    This is the central nervous system of the firmware. The `main()` function performs initial setup and then enters an infinite loop called `fw__vmt_handler()`. Think of this handler as a diligent receptionist constantly checking for new tasks for different departments (CM, RX, TX). When a request arrives, it dispatches the task to the appropriate handler function, which then processes it. This event-driven model allows the firmware to manage multiple hardware components concurrently without getting stuck waiting for one task to finish.
